-- title:
--   Module-finiteness of crossing-model quotients by ideals avoiding both branches
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $E$ be a natural number with $1 \le E$. Write $R$ for the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)`, that is, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0, X_1]]$ (formally, `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`) by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \pi^E$, and let $J$ be an ideal of $R$. Assume that $J$ is contained in neither of the two ideals $(\,\mathrm{const}(\pi),\, U\,)$ and $(\,\mathrm{const}(\pi),\, V\,)$ of $R$, where $\mathrm{const}(\pi)$ denotes the image of the constant power series $\pi$ and $U$, $V$ are the elements `U (π ^ E)` and `V (π ^ E)` of $R$ cutting out the two branches. Then the quotient ring $R/J$ is a finite $W$-module, i.e. finitely generated as a module over $W$ via the structure morphism.
--
--   This is the module-finiteness criterion for quotients of the completed local ring of a crossing (node) $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$ by an ideal meeting neither branch ideal $(\pi,U)$, $(\pi,V)$. It supplies the finiteness hypothesis used in the [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple`](def/ModularCurve_ProlongationTuple.html#L71) results comparing evaluations at points over a node with norms of quotients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_moduleFinite_quotient_of_not_le_span_pair.lean

